<title>USA: Echo Bay Mines Q4 shr loss widens.</title>
<headline>Echo Bay Mines Q4 shr loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>ECHO BAY MINES</p>
<p>	     (American and Toronto stock exchanges, symbol ECO)</p>
<p>				    Earnings Summary</p>
<p>U.S. dollars</p>
<p> THREE MONTHS ENDED DEC 31:    1996		   1995</p>
<p> Revenue			     $79,544,000	  $92,430,000</p>
<p>Net loss before special</p>
<p>    one-time charges	    ( 26,394,000)	 ( 5,178,000)</p>
<p> (a)Special one-time charges  ( 77,134,000)		    ---</p>
<p> Net loss			  ( 103,528,000)	 ( 5,178,000)</p>
<p>Weighted average common shares</p>
<p>  outstanding			139,351,704	  125,535,980</p>
<p> Loss per common share		 ( 0.74)		( 0.13)</p>
<p>TWELVE MONTHS ENDED DECEMBER 31:</p>
<p> Revenue				337,316,000	  360,730,000</p>
<p>Net loss before special</p>
<p>    one-time charges	    ( 69,568,000)	( 50,060,000)</p>
<p> (b)Special one-time charges ( 107,134,000)		    ---</p>
<p> Net loss			  ( 176,702,000)	( 50,060,000)</p>
<p>Weighted average common shares</p>
<p>  outstanding			134,434,054	  116,513,622</p>
<p> Loss per common share		 ( 1.31)		( 0.43)</p>
<p>(a) In the fourth quarter of 1996, the company wrote off its entire remaining investment in the Alaska-Juneau property, $57 million and established a reserve of $20 million to cover estimated reclamation and closure responsibilities.</p>
<p>(b) In the third quarter of 1996, the company established a one-time provision of $30 million for the estimated costs of stabilizing an unstable area of the pit wall at the McCoy/Cove mine. In addition, in the fourth quarter of 1996, the company took the actions described in footnote &quot;a.&quot;</p>
</text>
